# Backend Approved Task Rule

- Draft backend tasks as senior, implementation-ready specifications.
- Save a task under `tasks/backend/` only after the user explicitly approves it.
- Use lowercase kebab-case filenames ending in `.md`.
- Mark saved tasks with `Status: Approved` and the approval date.
- Include: objective, endpoint, contract, business rules, scenarios, error behavior, and acceptance criteria.
- Every response example must follow `[base_response.md](../../base_response.md)` with `meta`, `data`, `cache`, and `error`.
- Use `Accept-Language: en-US | ar-SA`; return one localized display value, never parallel `*En` and `*Ar` fields.
- Keep stable machine-readable status and reason codes separate from localized display text.
- Cover positive, blocking, mixed-state, empty, authorization, validation, concurrency, and idempotency scenarios when relevant.
- For multi-entity rules, identify each affected entity and explain whether it blocks the operation.
- Do not invent fields rejected by the user or expand an approved task without new approval.
- Use relative Markdown links only.
- Updating a task file does not update live architecture/API documents. Apply the repository documentation-sync rules separately when implementation specifications are promoted.
